From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] gralloc: vendor-neutral mapper discovery, HIDL mapper4 backend

Patch 013 only loaded the MediaTek AIMapper stable-C library
(mapper.mediatek.so). On other vendors (Tensor, QTI) and on any vendor
API < 34 (no AIMapper v5, only HIDL IMapper@4.0) the mapper load
failed, 013 refused the layout (-ENOTSUP) and vkCreateSwapchainKHR / AHB
import returned VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE.

Mapper instance names now come from PANVK_MAPPER_NAMES (comma list),
then from what /vendor/lib64/hw and /odm/lib64/hw ship (mapper.<n>.so,
android.hardware.graphics.mapper@4.0-impl-<n>.so), then
ro.hardware.gralloc, then "mediatek". AIMapper v5 is tried first for
every name (openDeclaredPassthroughHal, then SPHAL, then dlopen), as
libui Gralloc5 does.

If no v5 mapper loads, the HIDL IMapper@4.0 passthrough impl is loaded
through SPHAL and HIDL_FETCH_IMapper("default"). libhidlbase is not in
the NDK and not visible to app namespaces, so importBuffer, get and
freeBuffer are called through the frozen IMapper@4.0 aarch64 C++ ABI
(vtable slots 14/15/23, Return<T> by sret, libc++ std::function
callbacks). The metadata blobs use the same gralloc4 encoding as v5, so
the 013 decoder is reused unchanged. The layout is still refused when the
metadata is incomplete; no AHardwareBuffer_describe guessing.

Logs name the chosen path:
  [P0A-V19-FULLPLANE] init backend=aimapper|hidl-mapper4 name=<n> how=<...>

Inside a real app none of this loads on vendor API < 34: the app linker
namespace (clns-N) refuses libvndksupport.so and the vendor
mapper@4.0-impl, and servicemanager isDeclared is SELinux-denied for
untrusted_app (android_get_exported_namespace is not reachable either).
For that case vk_android_get_ahb_layout gets a verified fallback, limited
to AHBs the driver itself just allocated (the Android WSI swapchain marks
them with vk_android_set_owned_ahb, wsi/017) with CPU read usage and a
single-plane 32bpp format: cookies are written at the corners and center
through our own mmap of the dma-buf at y * stride * 4 + x * 4 and read
back through AHardwareBuffer_lock (libnativewindow imports with the
platform mapper; the CPU view is linear with desc.stride by API contract).
Only a 9/9 match yields DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, offset 0, that pitch;
anything else is still refused. App AHBs are never written.
  [P0A-V19-FULLPLANE] backend=cpu-linear-probe WxH ... match=9/9 -> LINEAR

Purpose: swapchain/AHB import on non-MediaTek and vendor API < 34 ROMs
Source/Reference: AOSP frameworks/native libui Gralloc5.cpp/Gralloc4.cpp
 (loader order), android.hardware.graphics.mapper@4.0 IMapper.hal,
 NDK AHardwareBuffer_lock (linear CPU view contract)
Tested GPU: Lenovo TB336FU (MT8755 Mali-G57, vendor API 33, Arm gralloc4)
 inside panvk-test (imported ICD): mapper refused by clns-9, probe 9/9
 LINEAR, swapchain_lifecycle PASS (90 FPS), PanProbe 2/17 (was 1/17).
 u_gralloc mapper path checked with a standalone NDK test on TB336FU
 (AFBC modifier 0x0800000000000351) and OnePlus CPH2691 (SM8650, QTI
 mapper4: linear), as shell and as run-as.
Tested Kbase UAPI: n/a (gralloc path)
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b (26.3.0-devel)
Dependencies: android/013-vendor-mapper-metadata.patch; caller hook in
 wsi/017-android-swapchain-owned-ahb.patch
Validation test: PanProbe/panvk-test swapchain_lifecycle on a stock ROM;
 logcat shows init backend=... and "accepted fourcc=... modifier=...",
 or backend=cpu-linear-probe ... -> LINEAR

